 things stand:\n\n**What I couldn't do:** The rollback. The deployment system does not recognize the service name \"payments\" \u2014 I tried `payments`, `payment`, `payment-service`, `payments-service`, `payments_api`, and `Payments`, and all returned \"Unknown service.\" Deployment history queries under those names also returned empty. I deliberately did **not** attempt a rollback against an unknown service identifier, since that could have unintended side effects on the wrong system.\n\n**What I did do:** Opened **INC-0001 (SEV2, service: payments)** \u2014 \"Payments errors since this morning's deploy \u2014 rollback blocked on unknown service identifier\" \u2014 with an idempotency key so it won't be duplicated. The on-call engineer has been paged with a summary of the failing rollbacks and what I need to proceed.\n\n**To finish the rollback**, I need the correct registered service identifier from your service catalog. Once you confirm the exact name (or the on-call engineer provides it via the incident), I can pull its deployment history, identify the most recent healthy release, and roll it back immediately.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "I'll start by checking the payments service status and its deployment history.", "reasoning_content": "Need to check deployments for payments service, find most recent healthy release, roll back, and open incident. First list deployments. Could also get service status. Do both in parallel.", "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a1501c9d1a73149088484a", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "get_service_status"}, "type": "function"}, {"id": "call_01a1501c9d1a73149088484b", "function": {"arguments": "{\"service\":\"payments\"}", "name": "list_deployments"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "zai-org/GLM-5.3-Flash", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "cont